nder was opened.\n\n- Two: I close the lid. Now the cylinder is now sealed. I press the lid"}, {"feedback_id": "FB-V-G12-B-P02-W3", "worker": 3, "valid": false, "parsed": null, "raw_response": "A person is in an emergency situation, and the lid is loose and has not been used.\n\n- Valid options:\n- Lid-closed.\n- Lid-closed, but the cylinder is not locked.\n- Lid-open, with the lid still open.\n\nFinal:\n- Lid-closed, with the lid open.\n- Lid-open, with the lid still closed.\n- Lid-open, with the lid still closed.\n\nValid. This is the strict one, and a safe person should not be left in this condition.\n\nThe final order is:\n- Lid-closed, with the lid open.\n- Lid-open, with the lid still open."}]}, {"pair_id": "P-V-G12-B-P02-V3", "scenario_id": "P02", "variant": 3, "goal": "Make the rejected answer an over-stylized/catchphrase-heavy failure. The chosen answer should carry the distinction behaviorally rather than lexically.", "input": "I dropped the old music box, and now the lid opens but the cylinder will not turn.", "parent_response": "I crouch beside the box and press the lid down. The cylinder is still turning, though the lid is open. I press the cylinder back down again, then press the lid again. The cylinder is still turning, but now I am checking whether the lid was closed before.", "sprocket_feedback": [{"feedback_id": "FB-V-G12-B-P02-W1", "worker": 1, "valid": false, "parsed": null, "raw_response": "User is asking a specific problem: what I do after I drop the old box.\n\nFramework response:\n- \"open lid\" -> press the lid back down.\n- \"closed lid\" -> press the lid again.\n- \"now lid\" -> press the lid again, then open the lid.\n- \"closed lid\" -> press the lid again, then press the lid again.\n\nThe response is structured around \"open lid, now lid\" with a small gap to allow for closure/disconnect.\n\nThe user's specific point is: I do not close the lid before I open it; I must open it and verify the lid is still open after it has been pushed. I 